The song appears in ''[[Romy and Michele's High School Reunion]]'' (1997), ''[[Harold & Kumar Escape from Guantanamo Bay|Harold and Kumar Escape from Guantanamo Bay]]'' (2008), ''[[Love & Other Drugs]]'' (2010),{{citation needed|date=March 2026}} the ''[[Black Mirror]]'' episode "[[San Junipero]]" (2016),<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bramesco |first=Charles |date=October 21, 2016 |title=Black Mirror Recap: Heaven Is a Place on Earth |url=https://www.vulture.com/2016/10/black-mirror-recap-season-3-episode-4.html |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=Vulture |language=en-us |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322024739/https://www.vulture.com/2016/10/black-mirror-recap-season-3-episode-4.html |url-status=live }}</ref> season 2 episode 6 of ''[[Dark (TV series)|Dark]]'' (2017), and it is sung by the protagonist June Osbourne in the [[The Handmaid's Tale (TV series)|''Handmaid's Tale'']] episode "Heroic" (2019).<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 19, 2019 |title=TV Recap: 'The Handmaid's Tale' Episode 9 – "Heaven is a Place on Earth" |url=https://awardswatch.com/tv-recap-the-handmaids-tale-episode-9-heaven-is-a-place-on-earth/ |access-date=March 4, 2023 |website=AwardsWatch |language=en-US |archive-date=March 4, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230304183340/https://awardswatch.com/tv-recap-the-handmaids-tale-episode-9-heaven-is-a-place-on-earth/ |url-status=live }}</ref> 

The song is referenced in [[Lana Del Rey]]'s 2011 debut single "[[Video Games (Lana Del Rey song)|Video Games]]".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Beviglia |first=Jim |date=June 12, 2020 |title=Behind The Song: Lana Del Rey, "Video Games" |url=https://americansongwriter.com/video-games-lana-del-ray-behind-the-song/ |access-date=December 22, 2022 |website=American Songwriter |archive-date=December 23, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221223010154/https://americansongwriter.com/video-games-lana-del-ray-behind-the-song/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The artist as well as the song are referenced in "Belinda Says", from Canadian band [[Alvvays]]' 2022 album ''[[Blue Rev]]''.{{citation needed|date=March 2026}}

The song was later included in the [[jukebox musical]] ''[[Head over Heels (musical)|Head over Heels]]'' that used the Go-Go's music in addition to two of Carlisle's solo tracks. The musical debuted on Broadway in 2018.{{citation needed|date=March 2026}}

sections.text:
The song appears in Romy and Michele's High School Reunion (1997), Harold and Kumar Escape from Guantanamo Bay (2008), Love & Other Drugs (2010),{{citation needed|date=March 2026}} the Black Mirror episode "San Junipero" (2016), season 2 episode 6 of Dark (2017), and it is sung by the protagonist June Osbourne in the Handmaid's Tale episode "Heroic" (2019). 

The song is referenced in Lana Del Rey's 2011 debut single "Video Games". The artist as well as the song are referenced in "Belinda Says", from Canadian band Alvvays' 2022 album Blue Rev.{{citation needed|date=March 2026}}

The song was later included in the jukebox musical Head over Heels that used the Go-Go's music in addition to two of Carlisle's solo tracks. The musical debuted on Broadway in 2018.{{citation needed|date=March 2026}}
